# Anomalous WinRM Session Source

## Overview

Surfaces devices that initiate a Windows Remote Management (WinRM / PowerShell Remoting) session for the first time within a rolling baseline period. Most lateral movement coverage sits on the destination side, watching for unusual logons arriving at a host. This query inverts that and looks at the origin: a workstation that has never spoken WinRM to anything and suddenly does is a meaningful signal, because outside of IT staff and management tooling the protocol is close to unused on client endpoints.

WinRM is the better half of this pair. Interactive remoting from a standard workstation is genuinely rare, which keeps the result set small enough to read by hand. The RDP equivalent lives in [Anomalous RDP Session Source](Anomalous_RDP_Source_Device.md) and is considerably noisier.

This is written as a hunting query, not a custom detection rule. See Why This Is a Hunt below before deploying it as an alert.

